      "message": "`folio_size(folio) \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB` is what `vma_folio_nr_ptes()` (`mm/p3s/rmap.h`, aosp/4390444) returns for a large folio in a 4KB VMA, and `folio_referenced_one()` and `try_to_unmap_one()` use it for the same \"fully mapped\" test before they restore the mlock. Would you mind using it here, so that `mlock_pte_range()` and the rmap walks agree on when a folio is fully mapped?\n\n```\n\telse if (!offset \u0026\u0026 nr \u003d\u003d vma_folio_nr_ptes(vma, folio))\n```\n\nIn the same way, the `pte_present()` and `vm_normal_folio()` tests in the loop are `p3s_pte_maps_folio()`.",
