      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `p3s_mlock_folio()` relies on its caller having checked the first PTE: `mlock_pte_range()` only calls it for a present PTE for which `vm_normal_folio()` returned `folio`, so its loop starts at `nr \u003d 1`. Here, though, nothing has looked at the PTE at `start`: it can be none, map another page, or, in a `MAP_PRIVATE` mapping, hold the swap or migration entry of a COWed slice.\n\nMost of these fall out at `!offset`, but arm64 keeps the swap offset in bits 12 and up, so `__pte_to_phys()` of such an entry returns the offset shifted by 12 rather than an address, and it could happen to match the folio. The folio would then be mlocked although its first slice isn\u0027t mapped here.\n\nWould you mind checking that PTE before the call, e.g. with `p3s_pte_maps_folio()` from `mm/p3s/rmap.h`? Something like:\n\n```\n\tpte -\u003d offset \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB;\n\tif (p3s_pte_maps_folio(vma, start, ptep_get(pte), folio))\n\t\tp3s_mlock_folio(folio, vma, pte, start, start + size);\n```",
